message: "If you use this study, please cite it using the metadata below and add the Zenodo DOI after deposition."
title: "Cosmological Recurrence Probability Study: A Fate-Conditioned Partial-Identification Framework"
type: software
date-released: 2026-08-09
authors:
  - family-names: Sundy
    given-names: Scott A.
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - recurrence
  - de Sitter
  - Poincare recurrence
  - dark energy
  - partial identification
  - DESI
abstract: >-
  A reproducible fate-conditioned framework separating observational parameter uncertainty,
  Bayesian model-family uncertainty, explicit ultimate-fate sensitivity, thermodynamic de Sitter
  recurrence scales, and finite-system quantum epsilon recurrence. Master study uses the current cited DES-Dovekie comparison evidence while retaining
  the DESI DR2+CMB two-model evidence weights and six-future fate decompositions and preserving
  the theory-agnostic recurrence-probability bound [0,1] as an explicit
  partial-identification/non-identifiability result rather than a probability estimate.
